The test failure indicates that the generated USB Audio Class 2 (UAC2) AudioControl (AC) interface descriptor does not match the expected reference descriptor. Specifically, the `wTotalLength` field, which is the total size of all class-specific AC interface descriptors, is incorrect.

This is caused by an error in the devicetree overlay file `tests/subsys/usb/uac2/app.overlay`. The `in_feature_unit` for the microphone path has its `data-source` property incorrectly set to `out_terminal`, which is the input terminal for the headphone path. The `out_terminal` has two audio channels.

The `in_feature_unit`'s controls are configured for a single-channel source (the microphone). This mismatch between the number of channels from the specified `data-source` (2 channels) and the feature unit's configuration (for 1 channel) leads to an incorrect calculation of the feature unit descriptor's size. This, in turn, results in an incorrect `wTotalLength` in the main AC interface header descriptor, causing the test to fail.

The fix is to correct the `data-source` of `in_feature_unit` to point to `mic_input`, which is the correct single-channel input terminal for the microphone path.

